<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!--
      Two permissions this app must never ship, held out of the merged manifest by
      name (BIT-57). Both are enforced rather than trusted because both can arrive
      without anyone in this repo typing them.

      ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION — the approved map rationale (DEV-54) says bittr needs
      your *approximate* location, matching iOS's kCLLocationAccuracyHundredMeters.
      Map and places SDKs routinely declare FINE in their own manifests, and the
      merger unions permissions: adding one dependency is enough to put "precise
      location" in the merged manifest, on the Play listing's permission list, and
      in the system dialog as a Precise/Approximate toggle — with no Kotlin change
      to review. A source scan cannot see that happen. This line can.

      RECORD_AUDIO — the approved scanner rationale (DEV-37) says nothing is
      recorded. CameraX's video artefact (androidx.camera:camera-video) declares
      RECORD_AUDIO, so pulling it in for any reason would advertise a recording
      capability on the store listing even before a line of code used it.

      RECORD_AUDIO's directive is still a no-op, which is the point: it is already in
      place for the merge that would otherwise introduce it. The location one stopped
      being a no-op at BIT-53 — `org.maplibre.gl:android-sdk` declares
      ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION in its own AAR manifest (verified against the published
      artefact, not its docs), so this line is now the only reason the shipped APK
      does not ask for precise location. That is not a MapLibre wart; every map SDK
      considered did it or recommended it, and it is why the choice was made against
      a test rather than against a comparison table.

      If one of these ever becomes genuinely necessary, the copy changes first and
      changed copy goes back through compliance — do not delete these lines to make a
      build pass. Asserted by LocationPrecisionGuardTest, MapSdkGuardTest and
      CameraCaptureGuardTest.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" tools:node="remove" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO" tools:node="remove" />

    <!--
      The one location permission this app ships (BIT-53, DEV-54). Coarse alone can
      only ever grant approximate location, whatever the user taps in the dialog,
      which is what keeps the shipped map copy true: "To centre the map on where you
      are, bittr needs your approximate location." It is the faithful port of iOS's
      kCLLocationAccuracyHundredMeters (Map/MapViewController.swift:80).

      Declared here rather than left to MapLibre's manifest so that the permission
      bittr does ask for is a decision in this repo, visible in this diff, next to
      the one it refuses.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" />

    <application
        android:name=".BittrApplication"
        android:allowBackup="false"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.Bittr">

        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            android:label="@string/app_name"
            android:theme="@style/Theme.Bittr">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>

</manifest>
